    ismot.p $e |- P = ( Base ` G ) $.
    ismot.m $e |- .- = ( dist ` G ) $.
    $( Property of being an isometry mapping to the same space.  In geometry,
       this is also called a motion.  (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux,
       15-Dec-2019.) $)
    ismot $p |- ( G e. V -> ( F e. ( G Ismt G ) <-> ( F : P -1-1-onto-> P
      /\ A. a e. P A. b e. P ( ( F ` a ) .- ( F ` b ) ) = ( a .- b ) ) ) ) $=
