       [Schwabhauser] p. 121.  Note that the textbook first defines a "strict"
       parallelism where equal lines are not considered parallel in the strict
       sense: here we jump directly to the more common definition which allows
       equality.  (Contributed by Thierry Arnoux, 17-Jun-2026.) $)
    df-prlng $a |- parlnG = ( g e. _V |-> { <. a , b >. | (
        ( a e. ran ( LineG ` g ) /\ b e. ran ( LineG ` g ) )
        /\ ( a = b \/ ( E. h e. ran ( PlnG ` g ) ( a C_ h /\ b C_ h )
        /\ ( a i^i b ) = (/) ) ) ) } ) $.
  $}

