    @d P i p @.
    @( The general upper dimension axiom for Euclidean geometry.  Given ` N `
       distinct points, the locus of all points equidistant from them forms a
       line in ` N ` dimensional geometry.  Derived from remarks in _Tarski's
       System of Geometry_, Alfred Tarski and Steven Givant, Bulletin of
       Symbolic Logic, Volume 5, Number 2 (1999), 175-214.  Note the similarity
       to ~ axlowdim . @)
